WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.290
hello I'm Nigel Lovell Martin and I

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.390
would like to introduce you to Patrick's

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.800
for level training evaluation model in

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.630
this presentation we will examine the

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.509
model and its applicability within the

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:20.580
broad field of instructional design the

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.380
four level model of evaluation was

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.710
developed by Donald Kirkpatrick in 1954

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.820
as the work of his doctoral dissertation

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.859
with relatively minor revisions the

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:34.620
model has remained the primary measure

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.750
in assessing the effectiveness of

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.980
training in business and industry this

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.020
log is not likely to be recommended in

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.789
planning programs in the K through 12

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:47.969
classroom but classroom teachers may use

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.190
this model if they are responsible for

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.320
planning training events within their

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.170
respective department or when planning

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.539
for adult learners in staff development

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.750
settings the four levels within the

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:05.450
model are reaction learning behavior and

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:10.590
results at the reaction level the focus

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.900
is on the reaction of the participants

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.229
to the training or the learning

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:18.900
experience at the learning level the

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.180
focus moves to the new learning that

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.840
results from the training at the

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.640
behavior level the focus is on the

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.820
transfer of learning and that the

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.040
results level the focus is on the

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.860
targeted outcomes that are expected as a

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.430
result of the training so in committing

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.650
this model to memory let us recap the

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.090
four levels in their order reaction

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:52.049
learning behavior and results let us

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:55.860
examine each of these levels level one

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.229
is the reaction level where we are

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:01.020
seeking to determine to what degree the

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.810
participants react favorably to the

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.229
training event we might ask participants

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:09.300
whether there is a feeling of

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.239
satisfaction or whether they are feeling

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:12.990
good about

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.530
training this is important because at

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.860
this level evaluation comes in the form

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:25.350
of feedback from participants at the

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.600
learning level we will determine the

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.070
degree to which participants have

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:32.370
acquired the intended knowledge skills

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.100
and attitudes based on their

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.150
participation in the learning event the

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.720
focus is on effective acquisition of the

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.770
content evaluating the effectiveness of

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.290
the learning at this level is done

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.660
through performance demonstration or

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.620
testing this is akin to a formative

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:02.130
evaluation or a formative assessment at

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.610
level three or the behavior level the

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.640
intent is to determine to what extent

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.490
participants can demonstrate transfer of

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.710
learning in the workplace

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.340
setting at this level we are looking for

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.030
evidence of change in job behavior as a

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.190
result of the training or the new

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:27.240
learning evaluation at this level takes

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.410
place post training it is recommended

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:35.430
that this be done at least three to six

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.880
months after the training event has

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.600
concluding and the evaluation is

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.900
primarily through observation looking

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:51.230
for change in participants job behavior

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.240
the final level in Donnell Kirkpatrick's

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.580
formulation of the model is the results

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.080
level an appropriate question might be

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.970
to what degree do targeted outcomes

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.390
occur as a result of the learning event

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:10.950
and a subsequent reinforcement the

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.400
results level allows for the defining of

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.548
specific measures that will be changed

00:04:17.548 --> 00:04:22.860
or improved as a result of the training

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.400
intervention evaluation at this

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.270
focuses on specific outcomes that were

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:35.850
targeted contemporary trainers who use

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.680
the Kirkpatrick modeling business and

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.190
industry always begin with the end in

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.259
mind

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:45.090
by this they mean the targeting of

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.270
desired outcomes the four training

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.770
begins they contend that evaluation in

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.370
the model frequently stops at level two

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:01.190
the learning level primarily because

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.350
evaluation at levels three and four are

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.130
difficult to measure

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.470
however with targeted outcomes in place

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.979
trainers often find it easier to conduct

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:17.400
evaluation at all levels including the

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.520
more difficult to measure transfer of

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:26.039
learning there will always be ideas for

00:05:26.039 --> 00:05:28.530
improvement when one works with a model

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:33.150
that is 60 years old some theorists in

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.389
the Patrick tradition have argued for a

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:38.630
fifth level

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.240
JJ Philips has proposed the return on

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.770
investment or the ROI level where he

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.229
compares level four or the result level

00:05:49.229 --> 00:05:52.830
with the cost of training in other words

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.560
Phillips might ask a question such as is

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.500
there a payoff for participating in

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:03.930
training a second theorist Raja Kaufmann

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.930
argues against return on investment as a

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.930
separate level and instead has

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:14.250
incorporated it into the results level

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.520
or level four where he believes it

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.960
rightfully belongs consequently Kaufman

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.169
has argued for a fifth level that will

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:27.810
focus on the impact of the organisation

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:31.710
on its external environment which

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.590
includes its clients and the members of

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:38.060
the wider society

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.090
as we conclude this presentation that is

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:44.770
recap what has been covered

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.210
Kirkpatrick's mode of evaluation is used

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.810
to assess the effectiveness of training

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:54.280
primarily in business and industry

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.930
evaluation is built-in at each of the

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.900
four levels of the model these levels

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.110
are reaction learning behavior and

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:08.300
results planning that uses the model is

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:12.039
done with the end in mind that is

00:07:12.039 --> 00:07:15.370
identifying targeted outcomes at the

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:19.449
results level even before embarking on

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:23.080
level 1 or the reaction level and

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:28.360
finally there have been arguments

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:32.449
advocating for the addition of a fifth

00:07:32.449 --> 00:07:39.050
model among contemporary traders for

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.840
additional information on this model you

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.590
may visit the online resource for

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:48.409
kirkpatrick partners using the link

00:07:48.409 --> 00:07:53.949
provided here thanks for watching

